      "note": "Missing guard: the statement `b += delim(input[b])` executes unconditionally regardless of input_length. When input_length == 0, b == 0 from the preceding loop that never executed, and input[0] is out of bounds. The fix adds `if (input_length)` before this statement.",
      "kind": "root_cause_line"
    },
    {
      "file": "lib/puny_decode.c",
      "function": "_idn2_punycode_decode",
      "line": null,
      "code": "",
      "note": "The expression delim(input[b]) unconditionally reads input[0] to check whether the character at position b is the Punycode delimiter (hyphen-minus, 0x2D). When input_length == 0, input[0] is beyond the valid buffer, reading uninitialized heap memory. MSAN reports the tainted result at line 166 where b is used in control flow.",
